    "question": "What is the main purpose of the letter?",
    "passage": "Pinnacle Property Management\n410 Granville Road, Eastbrook\n\nNovember 3\n\nDelia Fontaine, Owner\nFontaine Graphic Studio\nUnit 2B, Granville Commerce Center\n\nDear Ms. Fontaine,\n\nThis letter concerns the lease for Unit 2B at the Granville Commerce Center, which is set to expire on January 31. We are pleased to offer you a renewal under the following terms.\n\nShould you renew for two years, your monthly rent will increase by three percent, from $2,200 to $2,266. If you prefer a one-year term, the new monthly rent will be $2,310. In either case, all other conditions of your current lease, including the two reserved parking spaces and after-hours building access, will remain unchanged. As a returning tenant, you will also be given priority consideration should a larger unit become available during your new term; Unit 3A, which offers nearly double your current floor space, is expected to be vacant in June.\n\nPlease let us know your decision in writing by December 15. If we do not receive a response by that date, we will assume you do not wish to renew, and the unit will be listed publicly. Should you have questions or wish to discuss the terms, I am available at 555-0157 on weekdays.\n\nSincerely,\n\nRaymond Choi\nLeasing Manager\nPinnacle Property Management",
