    "passage": "Riverton Chamber of Commerce\n92 Union Square, Riverton\n\nSeptember 4\n\nMr. Khalid Mansour\nFounder, Mansour Bakery & Café\n310 Old Mill Road, Riverton\n\nDear Mr. Mansour,\n\nOn behalf of the Riverton Chamber of Commerce, it is my great pleasure to inform you that Mansour Bakery & Café has been selected to receive this year's Cornerstone Award, which honors a locally owned business that has made an outstanding contribution to the community. The selection committee was particularly impressed by your bakery's apprenticeship program, which has trained more than thirty young bakers over the past five years, and by your weekly donations of unsold goods to the Riverton Food Pantry.\n\nThe award will be presented at our annual Business Recognition Dinner on Friday, October 17, at the Grandview Hotel ballroom. The evening begins with a reception at 6:00 P.M., followed by dinner at 7:00 P.M. and the awards ceremony at 8:30 P.M. As an honoree, you will receive two complimentary tickets, and additional seats may be purchased for guests at $65 each. We kindly ask that you prepare brief remarks of no more than three minutes to deliver upon accepting the award.\n\nPlease confirm your attendance with my assistant, Joel Reyes, at 555-0119 by September 26. Congratulations on this well-deserved recognition.\n\nWarm regards,\n\nVivian Castellanos\nPresident, Riverton Chamber of Commerce",
