    "passage": "MEMO\n\nTo: All staff, Hadley & Moreau Consulting\nFrom: Irene Vasquez, Director of Operations\nDate: May 27\nSubject: Office relocation — important dates\n\nAs announced at last month's all-hands meeting, our lease at 300 Tower Plaza ends on July 31, and we will move to our new offices at the Solano Building, 125 Birchwood Avenue, during the last full week of July. Please review the schedule below carefully.\n\nBy Friday, July 18: Pack the contents of your desk into the labeled crates that facilities will distribute on July 14. Label each crate with your name and your new floor assignment, which team leads will circulate by July 7. Do not pack laptops or monitors; the IT department will transport all electronic equipment separately.\n\nJuly 21–25: Movers will transfer crates and furniture. During this week, all employees will work remotely. Client meetings scheduled for that week should be held by videoconference or moved to another date.\n\nMonday, July 28: The Solano Building officially opens for staff. Building access cards will be handed out in the first-floor lobby between 8:00 A.M. and 10:00 A.M. Your current Tower Plaza card will stop working on July 26.\n\nQuestions about the move should be directed to facilities@hadleymoreau.com rather than to your team lead. A list of frequently asked questions is posted on the company intranet.",
