    "question": "Why is the company changing its expense procedure?",
    "passage": "MEMO\n\nTo: All department heads\nFrom: Curtis Ohlsson, Chief Financial Officer\nDate: October 1\nSubject: New expense reporting procedure\n\nEffective November 1, all employee expense reports must be submitted through ClearLedger, the online platform we have adopted to replace paper forms. This change follows a three-month pilot in the sales department, during which reimbursement processing time fell from an average of eighteen days to five.\n\nUnder the new procedure, employees will photograph receipts with the ClearLedger mobile application at the time of purchase. The application automatically records the date, amount, and vendor, and assigns the expense to the correct project code. Department heads will receive reports for approval electronically and may approve or return them from any device. Once approved, reimbursements will be deposited directly into employee bank accounts within five business days.\n\nPlease note two important points. First, paper expense forms will no longer be accepted after October 31, with no exceptions. Second, employees must still retain original receipts for purchases over $500 and forward them to the accounting office, as required by our auditors.\n\nTraining webinars will be held on October 9, 15, and 22 at 2:00 P.M.; attendance at one session is mandatory for anyone who submits or approves expenses. Recordings will be available afterward on the intranet, but viewing a recording does not replace the attendance requirement.",
